{
  "case_id": "2016-16-605",
  "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Had Laroe filed the lawsuit against the Town of Chester, it would have been dismissed for lack of standing. However, Laroe claims that because it sought intervention under Rule 24(a)(2), that things are different. That's wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It sets up a difference between intervening on the defendant's side and the plaintiff's side. Intervening on the defendant's side under your scheme, that's easy, but not on the plaintiff's side. And why should there be that disuniformity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The best reading of Rule 24(a)(2) is that it requires an intervenor, as a right, to demonstrate that he has Article III standing by showing that he has a cognizable interest cognizable under Article III, and that it could be impaired by the disposition of the pending lawsuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are some things that do require standing, like seeking damages, filing a new claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why did they bother?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has done that in -- with a number of statutes. I think in those cases, the intervention would be -- and those intervenors would not be permitted to do something that would require standing without a subsequent assessment of -- of the standing of those intervenors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How does a defendant have standing? How does that work? What the government says is a defendant has standing because the judgment in the case may affect an interest of the defendant, a significant interest. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court had held, incorrectly we believe, that we lacked standing, and what the Second Circuit held was that the district court was wrong, as a matter of law, to require that inquiry in the first place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I mean, I don't see any more with the defendant, how you can find a defendant without standing on that basis? I mean, the reason I find it relevant is because I think the other side is arguing that an intervenor has to have standing in the sense that a defendant has to have standing, at least when you intervene on the side of the defendant, as most do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, not the difficulty of writing an opinion. I want to know is there such a think as defendants having or not having standing, and if there is such a thing, why and how. And if you don't know the answer right away, have you ever read anything on the topic, and what would you recommend?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, let's put aside the question of intervention. How can a defendant not have standing? I mean, I'm -- somebody sues me, so they are dragging me into court. I don't want to be in the court. I'm there because I'm the defendant. And then the court is going to turn around and say, well, you have to leave because you don't have standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Counsel, on -- on that score, why isn't that exactly the case we have here? The Plaintiff in this case, by way of relief, seeks a money damages for the taking. All right. That's his complaint, page 122 of the Joint Appendix. Your client, page 162, wants damages for itself. That's something that the Plaintiff could not have had standing to obtain for your client."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretsky",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: I think this goes to a key premise of the Petitioner's argument that I want to make sure to clarify. The Petitioner is arguing that once an intervenor comes in as an intervenor of right -- as of right, there can essentially be no limits on what that intervenor can do. And that's simply not true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Let's assume, for the sake of argument, that -- because I think, as I read the district court's opinion here, they assumed you were asking for judgment in your name, because they were treating you as a contract vendor or vendee, and they were saying, you don't have the right to have a judgment in your name."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can they join him, so long as they simply say, we want him to get his meal, or if -- if they seek meals in their own name, a judgment running as to them, do they have to show standing at that stage?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are there cases in which courts have controlled 24(a)(2) intervenors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Three points. First, a 24(a)(2) mandatory intervenor is a full party and can send thousands of subpoenas or document requests without the court ever finding out about them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Well, we don't disagree with that. Our only point is that they have much more power over 24(b) than they do over (a)(2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-605",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
